  <obo:IAO_0000116 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;type&lt;/b&gt;: class&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;is-a&lt;/b&gt;: Mucosa&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;preferred name&lt;/b&gt;: FM_live_02413&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;:documentation&lt;/b&gt;: Gray's 99:1724 - The mucosa of the inferior surface is thin, smooth and similar to the rest of the oral cavity.  The mucosa of the postsulcal part of the dorsum contains many lymphoid follicles.  In the presulcal part, the dorsal mucosa is thicker, adherent to muscular tissue covered by numerous papillae; consists of connective tissue and stratified squamous epithelium.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;synonym&lt;/b&gt;: KB_INSTANCE_69650, FM_live_02414, KB_AUTO-INSERT2_2257&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;non-English equivalent&lt;/b&gt;: KB_INSTANCE_69651, KB_AUTO-INSERT(3)_1581&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;constitutional part of&lt;/b&gt;: Tongue&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;regional part&lt;/b&gt;: Mucosa of oral part of tongue, Mucosa of pharyngeal part of tongue&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;constitutional part&lt;/b&gt;: Lamina propria of tongue, Epithelium of tongue</obo:IAO_0000116>
  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mucosa of tongue</rdfs:label>
</owl:Class>

